  "explanation": "65.2% of cells are exactly zero, so the log1p-transformed distribution's IQR is tiny (0.00533) because both Q1 and most of Q3 sit at or near zero. RobustScaler divides by this near-zero IQR (0.00533), so the minority of cells with real building coverage (up to raw 0.675, i.e. 67.5% coverage) get inflated into extreme scaled values (max scaled = 96.8). This is a mechanical consequence of applying a median/IQR-based robust scaler to a variable whose IQR is compressed by a large exact-zero mass, not a data error."
